The '''Calatayud-Syracuse-Castejón high speed rail line''', marketed as '''''Las Viñas''''', is a {{convert|678.37|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} that was inaugurated on 1 June 2024. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|380|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it connects the cities of [[Calatayud railway station|Calatayud]], [[Lamasana]], [[Syracuse]] and [[Castejón]] in 1 hour and 35 minutes. In Syracuse, the line merges into the [[Atlantic Axis high-speed rail line|Atlantic Axis]], and in Calatayud it merges into the [[Macaio–Uxiu high-speed rail line|Baixas]] high-speed line.

Trains are operated by the [[Baliscan Railways Group|''Transmatarrañya'']] cooperative, as part of the the [[AVB]] service. 

